{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:ad3a4bd9344ce557","name":"Quick Draw","source":{"id":"source:reference-ad3a4bd9344ce557","title":"Quick Draw","revision":24964,"timestamp":"2024-11-10T16:18:53Z","sha256":"f40159776633647d3dac4192e50f706647b29968d28db5c00aa372248ba2ec36","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24964","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Quick%20Draw&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-ad3a4bd9344ce557","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["You can draw and holster weapons with startling quickness.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Prerequisite:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"}," +1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Effect:"]}," You can ",{"tag":"a","children":["Draw or Holster a Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Draw_or_Holster_a_Weapon","referenceId":"reference:2f721b5ad4f7aaff"}," as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," instead of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Combined Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Combined_Feat"},":"]}," If you have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dual Weapon Mastery I"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dual_Weapon_Mastery_I","referenceId":"reference:f50ca7ec9196bfe9"}," Feat, You can draw or holster two weapons with a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},"; you must have both hands free to draw both weapons, and each weapon must be able to be held in one hand. Additionally, if you have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Lightsabers)"}," Feat, you can draw and ignite ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," as a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Jedi Counseling"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Counseling"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Counseling"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," If a Jedi had the Quick Draw Feat and wanted to draw their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},", would they still have to use another ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," to activate the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},"?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," No. The \"",{"tag":"a","children":["Draw a Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Draw_a_Weapon"},"\" Action normally includes everything necessary to render that weapon immediately usable, including deactivating the safety on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:38dcc06542ba096c"}," and activating a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vibroblade"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vibroblade","referenceId":"reference:4d5963781a5121d7"},". Weapons are designed to be drawn and armed very quickly, so the GM generally shouldn't require a separate ",{"tag":"a","children":["Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Action"}," unless there's some unusual difficulty in play (such as when the wielder isn't proficient with the weapon). Similarly, you don't have to spend a separate ",{"tag":"a","children":["Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Action"}," to deactivate or disarm a weapon when you holster it.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["However, it is important to note that this applies only to the actual \"",{"tag":"a","children":["Draw or Holster a Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Draw_or_Holster_a_Weapon","referenceId":"reference:2f721b5ad4f7aaff"},"\" Action (that is, moving the weapon either to or from a holster, hanger, sling, and so on). It does not apply when picking up or dropping a weapon, nor does it apply when using the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," Skill to use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sleight of Hand"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand"}," to get the weapon in your hand without attracting attention. In these cases, you're not getting the weapon in your hand as efficiently as you would when drawing or holstering it.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
